A||||2||Cheever2||Tell me how to clean taillights||||2||
Z||000000||Cheever2||04-30-2001||09:21 AM||||Maybe I didn't look hard enough, but a quick search found nothing on this.  <P>The GT taillights I got from the parts car are very grimy.  Kinda frosty looking, but whatever it is, it's stuck on pretty good.  Similar to overspray of white paint, but I don't think so.  <P>I was about to first try soap & water, but sometimes the obvious to me turns out isn't such a good idea, so coming to the pro's before I do anything.<P>Also, do the outer covers come off the way it looks like they do?  Looks like several clips where you just have to pry up the plastic a little.<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000001||1988LRC||04-30-2001||09:28 AM||||to clean tailights or turn signals first use soap and water to remove the dirt, to remove scratches and haze start with 600 grit wet paper (and lots of water) then 800 then 1200 then 1500 after that use polishing compound for the final cleaning if you want you can put a coat of wax on when finished||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierosound||05-01-2001||01:02 AM||||Just did mine using the information at the Fiero Online Service Guide. They look like new!<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/taillights.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/taillights.html</A> <BR>||||reg||10
